  "UNITS": {
    "Furnace": {
      "Unit Description": "The furnace is a utility unit that can supply heat at very high temperatures (> 500\u00b0C) to industrial processes such as sintering, curing, metallurgical and thermal treatments, among other applications.The furnace model converts the chemical energy of a fuel into the thermal energy of hot flue gases by burning the fuel with air.",
      "Unit Info": {
        "Unit name": "Furnace",
        "Minimum capacity multiplier": 0.0,
        "Maximum capacity multiplier": 100.0
      },
      "Connectors Description": "The energy consumed by the furnace in the form of natural gas (in kW) is imported through the NATURALGAS layer from the natural gas supply grid located in the market model or produced by a methanation or an anaerobic digestion with purification process. In turn, the CO_{2} released from the flue stack that is susceptible to be captured in a flue gas purification unit can be sent to it through the CO2inFlueGas layer. The CO_{2} emissions arisen from the leakages of the hot gases are, in turn, sent to the environment through the layer EnvCO2em.",
